# Beads Issue Tracking
# Auto-generated by 'bd setup cursor' - do not remove these markers
# BEGIN BEADS INTEGRATION

This project uses [Beads (bd)](https://github.com/gastownhall/beads) for durable issue tracking.

## Core Rules

- Track shared project work in `bd` (not markdown TODOs / TodoWrite)
- Prefer the **`bd` CLI** when shell is available — it is the primary path for Claude Code and Codex here too
- Run `bd prime` when Beads context is missing or after compaction
- Commit / `bd dolt push` / git push only when the user, orchestrator, or active profile authorizes it (this repo uses the conservative/minimal profile)
- Do **not** re-run `bd setup claude` or `bd setup codex`, and do not add Beads MCP to Claude Desktop — those stay CLI + hooks / skill

## Quick Reference

```bash
bd prime                 # Load workflow context (SSOT)
bd ready                 # Unblocked work
bd show <id>             # Inspect before editing
bd update <id> --claim   # Claim atomically
bd create --title="..." --type=task --priority=2
bd close <id>            # Complete
```

## Cursor MCP

Project MCP server `beads` is registered in `.cursor/mcp.json` (`beads-mcp`). Prefer CLI for routine work; use MCP tools when structured tool calls are clearer. Do not configure a second Beads MCP elsewhere for this project.

## Workflow

1. `bd ready` / `bd show <id>`
2. `bd update <id> --claim`
3. Do the work
4. `bd close <id>`
5. Handoff: report files, validation, issue status; propose sync/commit only if authorized

Full operational detail: `bd prime`. Claude/Codex keep their existing hooks and skill; this rule is Cursor-only.

